description:
What: After Config is loaded in crates/smtp/src/main.rs, decode the DKIM key bytes and construct an Option<Arc<DkimSigner>> to pass to both queue constructors.

Algorithm:
1. After the config.delivery.smtp_relay_peers secretx resolution block (line ~158), add:
   let dkim_signer: Option<Arc<mail_auth::dkim::DkimSigner>> = if let Some(ref dcfg) = config.delivery.dkim {
       use base64::Engine as _;
       use zeroize::Zeroize as _;
       let seed = match base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD.decode(&dcfg.key_seed_b64) {
           Ok(b) => b,
           Err(e) => { eprintln!("error: dkim key_seed_b64: invalid base64: {e}"); std::process::exit(1); }
       };
       if seed.len() != 32 { eprintln!("error: dkim key_seed_b64: must decode to 32 bytes"); std::process::exit(1); }
       let pubkey = match base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD.decode(&dcfg.public_key_b64) {
           Ok(b) => b,
           Err(e) => { eprintln!("error: dkim public_key_b64: invalid base64: {e}"); std::process::exit(1); }
       };
       if pubkey.len() != 32 { eprintln!("error: dkim public_key_b64: must decode to 32 bytes"); std::process::exit(1); }
       let ed_key = mail_auth::dkim::Ed25519Key::from_seed_and_public_key(&seed, &pubkey);
       let mut seed = seed; seed.zeroize();
       let signer = mail_auth::dkim::DkimSigner::from_key(ed_key)
           .domain(&dcfg.domain)
           .selector(&dcfg.selector)
           .headers(["From", "To", "Subject", "Date", "Message-ID", "MIME-Version"])
           .canonicalization(mail_auth::dkim::Canonicalization::Relaxed, mail_auth::dkim::Canonicalization::Relaxed);
       info!(domain=%dcfg.domain, selector=%dcfg.selector, "DKIM signing enabled");
       Some(Arc::new(signer))
   } else {
       info!("DKIM signing disabled (no dkim config)");
       None
   };
2. Pass dkim_signer.clone() to NntpQueue::new() (after this bead, NntpQueue::new accepts it — b1bc.4).
3. Pass dkim_signer to SmtpRelayQueue::new() (after b1bc.5).

Defensive programming:
- Zeroize seed bytes immediately after key construction (step 1 includes this).
- ERROR messages for invalid base64/wrong length must NOT include the actual seed content.
- eprintln + exit(1) pattern matches rest of main.rs error handling.
- Log only domain+selector (never seed_b64 or public_key_b64).

Tests: Integration — start with valid config and DKIM config set; verify server starts and info log shows DKIM enabled.
